    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured `OWNER_CREATED` audit event by adding one new, self-contained aspect \u2014 matching the repo's established \"small standalone aspect\" convention \u2014 without modifying any existing class or method.\n\n**New file:** `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/OwnerCreatedEventAdvice.java`, containing two small cohesive units:\n\n- **`OwnerCreatedEventAdvice`** \u2014 an `@Around` aspect on `ClinicService.saveOwner(..)`. It captures `isNew()` before proceeding (so only genuine creates emit), then logs the event on the existing `AUDIT` logger. A single `AtomicLong seq` field gives a monotonically increasing integer across creates.\n- **`OwnerCreatedEvent`** \u2014 an immutable `record` rendering the JSON `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event:'OWNER_CREATED'}`.\n\n**Forward-compatibility with the memberId unification:** the event's identifier is read straight from `owner.getCustomerCode()` and passed as the record's generic `identifier`. When the customerCode is later unified into the memberId, the owner's primary identifier changes at its source and the event carries the memberId automatically \u2014 no change needed to this aspect.\n\n**Why this keeps structural impact low:** I touched exactly one file and added no complexity to any existing function or class (WMC_other of the surrounding aspect classes is untouched). Both new units are tiny: `emitCreatedEvent` has CC 2, and the record's methods have CC 1\u20132, each with near-zero surrounding context. The structured event lives beside \u2014 not inside \u2014 the existing plain audit line, so `OwnerAuditCreationAdvice` was left entirely alone.\n\nBoth the structured event and the original audit line now appear on the `AUDIT` logger:\n```\nAUDIT - {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\nAUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E registrationDate=2026-09-01 membershipLevel=1 membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M27\n```",
